  "scope": "The actual raw blowup ring projection is surjective, has its genuine two-sided kernel ideal, and gives the canonical VF integration quotient by that ideal. The free-ring semiring groupification is proved equivalent to additive Grothendieck completion for arbitrary semirings; equality of positive generators is exactly stable additive equality. Lifting the stabilization through a surjective semiring map proves an exact positive-pair kernel description, with no cancellation assumed in the original semirings. The raw volume kernel is then proved to be generated by actual equal-degree common-blowup differences. Point minus cone lies in the kernel, and every elementary difference from a source of degree at least two is its explicit left multiple. The single-generator converse in degree one remains open. Actual degree-one points with distinct absolute densities remain distinct under common blowups; this does not assert separation after groupification. Independently, every positive RV coordinate permutation with its inverse determinant density gives a full volume isomorphism. Its additive correction restores raw total integrals for ordinary and positive AE family inputs. Ordinary covariance is proved through genuine unit-density VF realizations. Appending selected coordinates preserves the determinant sign. These are exact signed covariance identities, not a claim of the remaining full raw coordinate-pushforward/Fubini assembly or ordinary-input raw Jacobian assembly. The accepted nonempty-selected-E scope and ordinary RV[0] convention are unchanged.",
